  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "SresZ9AINM6YRDaWk9Hg5y6ZjOI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:34:08.622Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Where your code runs decides how you obtain an `IReactorClient`. In React, you never construct one \u2014 you read the running reactor's client off a hook:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useReactorClient } from \"@powerhousedao/reactor-browser\";\n\nconst client = useReactorClient();\n```\n\n`@powerhousedao/reactor-browser` exposes a matching hook for each major subsystem, so the whole reactor graph is reachable from an editor or drive app without threading anything through props:\n\n- `useSync()` \u2014 the `ISyncManager`, or `undefined` when sync was never wired.\n- `useSyncList()` \u2014 its remotes (`Remote[]`).\n- `useModelRegistry()` \u2014 the document-model registry.\n- `useDatabase()` \u2014 the Kysely database.\n- `usePGlite()` \u2014 the PGlite instance.\n\nOutside React there are two other routes. **Standalone** (scripts, tests, servers) uses `ReactorClientBuilder`: wire a reactor with `.withReactorBuilder(builder)` or `.withReactor(reactor, eventBus, documentIndexer, documentView)`, add `.withSigner(...)` / `.withDocumentModelLoader(...)`, then `.build()`. `buildModule()` throws if neither `withReactorBuilder` nor `withReactor` was set.\n\n**In a generated subgraph**, the client is a property on the class: `BaseSubgraph` holds it as `reactorClient`, and `getResolvers(subgraph)` reads it off the instance. The GraphQL resolver `context` does **not** carry the reactor.\n\n**In a generated processor**, the client is `module.client` \u2014 but the factory parameter is typed as the base `IProcessorHostModule`, which exposes `relationalDb`, `analyticsStore`, `dispatch`, and `getReadModel` and *not* `client`. Widen it to reach the client:\n\n```typescript\nconst { client } = module as IReactorProcessorHostModule;\n```\n\nOne import-path caveat: reactor-browser re-exports only a curated subset of reactor types. `ViewFilter`, `SearchFilter`, `PagingOptions`, `JobInfo`, `JobStatus`, `IReactor`, `ReactorEventTypes`, and `SyncEventTypes` are not among them \u2014 import those from `@powerhousedao/reactor`.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/01-WorkingWithTheReactor.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:34:07.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:34:08.622Z"
    }
  },
